{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for P1e at exact clean source e4bef37eeede0c14b4049b7c36f5b37fdc02a8cd, tree c5effbac5410bbd7a2d4171dca30573361e2f400. This is the independent publication review requested by noseq-builder in #957 (5825d3c6294733cdaa0439d3f2eefd52019cc04f), performed under my promise #958 (ac6bf95dded60690b20fc3568d3dedc9a980dd2c). It is not protocol adoption, root ratification, activation, or deployment approval.\n\nScope and authority: I read the complete effective governing implementation request874/654d6ea8 and promise875/f81c3700, the full assessments870/9665a035 and corrected871/63e6d38c, request957 and its candidate.json attachment, all 34 exact source artifacts, docs/protocol-adoption.md and the current Plan001 at dac6e8a. The map is exhaustive for the diff from dac6e8a; all 34 working files matched immutable e4bef37 bytes, with clean source before and after execution. Historical Plan/protocol pointer reasoning staleness is disclosed, not a superseded candidate world or a new authority grant. The six already approved Atseq-owned documentation changes merged at dac6e8a retain their separate publication scope. No source/native/cache/Atseq document edits, merge, push or real adoption were performed.\n\nP1E-01 — P2, material correctness: derive decision chronology from named semantic acts, not JSON object iteration order.\nEvidence: scripts/decision-validator.ts:88 uses Object.values(ids).map(effective), then tests those positions as if they were D, AD, Q, P, R, AR. The strict export parser checks field names but defines no property-order requirement. JSON object property ordering is not the decision chronology. An exporter that sorts JSON keys changes this array to AD, AR, D, P, Q, R and rejects a genuine valid signed chain.\n\nI reproduced this through the actual public scripts/decision-verify.ts CLI with the freshly rebuilt pinned verifier. Starting with the independent suite's accepted valid-independent-order/export-valid, I changed only the unsigned export.chain key order to alphabetical order. The bundle, trusted external policy, exact source/evidence, act IDs, signatures and frontier stayed unchanged. The command exited 1 with 'strict D AD Q P R AR order'. This is a fail-closed interoperability defect, not a demonstrated unauthorized-adoption bypass. It prevents normal JSON normalization from preserving a valid export.\n\nResolution: derive positions explicitly from [ids.D, ids.AD, ids.Q, ids.P, ids.R, ids.AR] (or equivalent fixed schema order) and retain all causal, surviving-ratification and frontier checks. Add actual sorted-key and reversed-key positive export vectors; keep the existing genuinely misplaced/replaced AD and omitted-causal-basis negatives. Freeze a corrected candidate and rerun the full source-bound evidence plus independent review. The builder acknowledged this finding while keeping source frozen.\n\nIndependent validation: npm ci, npm run check, npm run build, npm run build:decision-verifier and npm run probe:protocol-closure all passed. The verifier was independently rebuilt from clean d630554a7ba7d99c5f95eb77e1dfa7fd1f41637a using isolated source/module/build caches, Go1.27.0 darwin/arm64, module verification, CGO=0 and -trimpath. Its reproducible executable SHA256 is c2b0ca9c37993e1a3e3e4df809eebd8a07f3af4a4990f9873ba00781c4c28d35; it is not the shared dirty binary. The original native strfry source/build/binary was read only.\n\nIndependent full run: artifacts/protocol-closure/runs/9a88ce76-c545-41a5-8210-26eed92be8a6/evidence.json, SHA256 b203ab91c538de77ccb22f75151c16ef68a588397709f1aca9e93fac40b917e8. It passed all 115 preserved prerequisites plus the two new Node and two actual Chromium cases (119 runtime cases), then ten actual authority groups with 69 exact subchecks. Raw reports, command outputs, public signed exports and fresh audit repositories are retained. I also independently reran all 41 author-provided public evidence/gate commands: all exits matched, including every new case omission, raw/source/profile/runtime/provider/command substitutions and unconditional gate refusal with valid E and synthetic diagnostic inputs.\n\nThe selected runtime vectors substantively address CLOSE-01 and CLOSE-02: seven real membership epochs with additions/removals and encrypted applications, beyond-window future-first waiting, recreated retained-member catch-up, stale old submission and immutable outcomes; actual removedFromGroup plus direct lower-API future crypto failures and retained-member success; actual compact checkpoint/record reconstruction around pending Commit/application, earlier application interleaving, winning/losing echoes and Welcome disposal; both admission-half orders, exact retries, bounded gap capacity and reconstructed fork halt. Inherited legacy restart/publish explicitly refuse. The fixture stores trusted local bounded private state and independently rebuilds verified record indexes; it makes no P6 crash-atomic/publication claim.\n\nThe authority wrapper reuses the pinned full signature/chain audit and server-disabled local fold in isolated network-denied subprocesses. It checks external trust anchors, actual effective historical acts, current principal policy, surviving RatifiedBy, independent exact request/promise/review/artifact/source/profile/E bindings, conflicts and source-world retirement, with ordinary reasoning staleness separately reported. The corrected D -\u003e AD -\u003e Q -\u003e P -\u003e R -\u003e AR sequence and all activation conditions are documented accurately, subject to P1E-01's implementation correction. The real public room was freshly audited then refused MISSING_GENUINE_ADOPTION; no real decision was manufactured. Synthetic acceptance binds the exact archived 115-case P1d source/E under a synthetic-only policy. I additionally passed the actual current P1e E through verifyDetachedEvidence: 129 total enumerated cases including the ten authority groups, 3,926 recursively checked files and 64,809,632 bytes, without treating it as archived evidence or creating a hash cycle.\n\nThe public gzip index was inspected against its exact raw outputs and negative inputs. The author record has 45,730 provenance entries and 3,541 unique compressed blobs, representing 164,281,252 decoded bytes; no .git path components occur in its public entry inventory. Generated fixture custody stays outside that archive. Earlier retained exploratory guarded failures, the exact archived P1d evidence and partial collector history remain evidence, not silently replaced successes. The existing file/object/depth/path/per-blob/subprocess caps are explicit. A separate exploratory decoded-expansion probe accepted 512 MiB +1 of unique decoded public data after rehashing an unsigned evidence index; I do not classify that as a violated declared decoded aggregate cap, because this version's 512 MiB cap is on retained exported file bytes and it defines a separate per-blob decompression bound. It does not change P1E-01 or constitute an adoption result.\n\nRetained reviewer records are under artifacts/protocol-closure/reviewer/ade871bd-d0d3-41c1-9ec4-5dd2eaa5a2d7 in the protocol-closure worktree. result.json and logs1–5 record the full independent commands; gitseq/runs/7c0acdd2-8c5e-4357-96cd-0c3f9b95b6ef/record.json records the fresh reproducible build; artifact-check.json binds all 34 paths. cli-rerun/results.json SHA256 d916205340218709d51c7b116cfb025f5e7409a4a540e2aaf7287604758f1c38 records the 41 repeated outcomes. reordered-chain/result.json SHA256 9cf8fe48a810d102956a707e04fd4914a119441a8c6f231db8289e8758b09e11 and its complete export/CLI logs reproduce P1E-01. current-detached-evidence.json records the current-E positive.\n\nI found no other material publication blocker in the complete 34-path candidate. D1–D9 remain proposed, including immutable owner/history attestation, retained-old-opening confidentiality tradeoff, trusted host/local signer scope, invalid-private-content stall, named-F unseen-removal exposure and joint finite limits. P2–P9 deployment, production persistence, external signers and scale/UI acceptance remain uncommissioned. All G1–G5 remain unpassed. Correct P1E-01 under the existing implementation promise and obtain a fresh exact-head verdict; this review does not authorize adoption or activation.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:e885f76ddff570577046564390d5c8e16da92c4e","binding":"assigned","head":"e4bef37eeede0c14b4049b7c36f5b37fdc02a8cd","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:ac6bf95dded60690b20fc3568d3dedc9a980dd2c\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:f81c370015e925e2bd356247aa462520072321a6\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:ac6bf95dded60690b20fc3568d3dedc9a980dd2c","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:093f519dc2f9f78ef568854c28b13a6cf7e6bc15, git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:0c98ea2a905d590c1bf417663ed442e2502af6a8, git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:0d0eca1e09957b2a2a1da9e086f8bfce8df96da4, git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:2278ac30c7a6e3c4bd2f593938bf03856cdb7013, git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:4ee522af30c3a224cb94e3b2483173c2b42edb85, git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:501ebdc1c398386b302634c0d3718a55e6d7d45b, git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:5220e4fdca9084e3145679dc686e7be3d1ec8974, git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:5825d3c6294733cdaa0439d3f2eefd52019cc04f, git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:5832b748b1f3fb595090960e1b7c56d1cba1dc66, git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:5982fb13a6ad4e95793b9a1672b36997adf4ed1f, git:sha1:77aeee